# Line-ending policy.
#
# Why this file exists: dist/ is committed and the README requires a rebuild in
# the same commit as any src/ or public/ change. On Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, git checks dist/ out as CRLF while `astro build` writes
# LF, so every rebuild reported ~79 modified files whose real diff was
# 0 insertions and 0 deletions. That made the "is dist/ in sync?" check —
# the one gate protecting the published site from drifting out of step with
# source — unreadable on Windows, and indistinguishable from genuine drift.

# Normalise everything to LF in the repository, and let git decide what is text.
* text=auto

# dist/ is generated output. Pin it to LF in the working tree as well, so it
# matches byte-for-byte what the build writes and never shows as modified.
dist/** text eol=lf

# Binary assets. These MUST come after dist/** — the last matching pattern
# wins, and applying `text` to them would corrupt them on checkout.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.avif  binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf   binary
